{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Blot me out, I pray.</b> Rashi explained: from the entire Torah. And it is surprising, for the Torah had not yet been written. Rashbam explained: ״from Your book״ — this is the Book of Life, in which a person is written on Rosh HaShanah. And thus we say in Rosh HaShanah: ״מספרך״ — these are the intermediate ones; ״אשר כתבת״ — these are the righteous. Another interpretation: If You do not forgive them, then how will You forgive [me for] Your tablets that I broke? If You forgive me, forgive them, for there is no favoritism in the matter. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: ״מי אשר חטא לי״ etc. — that is, they caused [this] for you, and the breach is theirs; but you acted rightfully, for they were not worthy to receive the tablets. Even so, he was erased from the entire parashah of ואתה תצוה, in which Moses is not mentioned, because cursing a sage takes effect even on condition."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:34.498862869Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}